 ork with the KB's collections\, facilities and expertise\, including its l
 arge digitised and born-digital holdings. Artists are explicitly eligible\
 , both for artistic production as a research strategy and for research ahe
 ad of production\, though NIAS provides no studio\, materials or tools.\n\
 nOrganisation: NIAS-KNAW (Netherlands Institute for Advanced Study) with t
 he KB\, National Library of the Netherlands\nLocation: Amsterdam (NIAS) wi
 th access to the KB in The Hague. Present 4 days a week.\nAward: Personal 
 stipend (figure not published)\; scholars at Dutch institutions get a Dutc
 h University Grant paid to their institution instead. Office\, subsidised 
 Amsterdam housing where eligible (otherwise local transport reimbursement)
 . No application fee.\nDuration: 5 months\, September 2027 to end of Janua
 ry 2028\n\nMore: https://nias.knaw.nl/fellowships/kb-fellowship?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
