SUMMARY:Deadline: Epistemics Fund (sponsored by Ought\, via Lightcone Commo
 ns): grants for tools that help people find what is true (USD 500\,000 to 
 5 million pool)
DESCRIPTION:A one-off fund for epistemics: tools and projects that help peo
 ple work out what is true. AREAS: community notes (including AI note write
 rs and rating tools)\; notes beyond social media (podcasts\, papers\, vide
 o\, the open web)\; provenance tracking (C2PA support\, reverse video sear
 ch\, synthetic-frame detection)\; reliability tracking of public figures\;
  forecasting and prediction markets\; decision and...\n\nOrganisation: Oug
 ht\, organised by Nathan Young on Lightcone Commons\nLocation: Open intern
 ationally\; no location requirement stated. Grants can go to individuals\,
  for-profits and US 501(c)(3) nonprofits.\nAward: Ought plans to make betw
 een USD 500\,000 and USD 5 million in grants in total to the top-ranked ap
 plications (the page writes '$'\; US dollars assumed). No fixed grant size
 : evaluators rank applications and funders decide how much each receives. 
 Example asks on the page range from 150\,000 to 1 million. No application 
 fee.\nDuration: Per project\; not stated\n\nMore: https://epistemic.fund/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://epistemic.fund/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
LOCATION:Open internationally\; no location requirement stated. Grants can 
 go to individuals\, for-profits and US 501(c)(3) nonprofits.
END:VEVENT
